fix(theme): suppressHydrationWarning on theme wrapper div

Skeptical-reviewer finding: server prerenders className="dark"
(initialTheme()'s SSR fallback). On the client, the useState
initializer reads localStorage and may pick 'light'. Without
suppressHydrationWarning React 19 flags this as a hydration
mismatch — exactly the case the warning is designed to silence.

Inline comment explains the invariant so future editors don't
remove it.


